  "description": "<h2>Maximum Number of Distinct Elements After Operations</h2><p>You are given an integer array <code>nums</code> and an integer <code>k</code>.</p>\n\n<p>You are allowed to perform the following <strong>operation</strong> on each element of the array <strong>at most</strong> <em>once</em>:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Add an integer in the range <code>[-k, k]</code> to the element.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Return the <strong>maximum</strong> possible number of <strong>distinct</strong> elements in <code>nums</code> after performing the <strong>operations</strong>.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<h3>Examples:</h3><ul><li><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [1,2,2,3,3,4], k = 2<br><strong>Output:</strong> 6<br><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><code>nums</code> changes to <code>[-1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4]</code> after performing operations on the first four elements.</p></li><li><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [4,4,4,4], k = 1<br><strong>Output:</strong> 3<br><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>By adding -1 to <code>nums[0]</code> and 1 to <code>nums[1]</code>, <code>nums</code> changes to <code>[3, 5, 4, 4]</code>.</p></li></ul><h3>Constraints:</h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 10<sup>9</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>0 &lt;= k &lt;= 10<sup>9</sup></code></li>\n</ul>\n",
